spans.s:
1. अर्च् cl. 1. P. अ॑र्चति (Subj. अ॑र्चात्; impf. आ॑र्चत्; aor. आर्चीत्, Bhaṭṭ.; perf. आनर्च, 3. pl. आनर्चुः [MBh. iii, 988, &c.], but Ved. आनृचुः॑ [RV.]; perf. Ā. (Pass.) आनर्चे [Bhaṭṭ.], but Ved. स॑म् आनृचे [RV. i, 160, 4]; fut. p. अर्चिष्यत् [Mn. iv, 251]; ind.p. अर्च्य [Mn. &c.; cf. Pāṇ. vii, 1, 38, Sch.] or अर्चित्वा [R. iii, 77, 15]; Ved. Inf. ऋच॑से [RV. vi, 39, 5 & vii, 61, 6]) to shine, be brilliant, RV.;
to praise, sing (also used of the roaring of the Maruts, and of a bull [RV. iv, 16, 3]), RV.; AV.; ŚBr., to praise anything to another (dat.), recommend, RV.;
to honour or treat with respect, MBh. &c.;
to adorn, VarBṛS. : exceptionally Ā. (1. pl. अर्चामहे)
to honour, MBh. ii, 1383:
Caus. (2. sg. अर्चयस्) to cause to shine, RV. iii, 44, 2. P. Ā. to honour or treat with respect, Mn.; MBh. &c.:
Desid. अर्चिचिषति, to wish to honour, Pāṇ. vi, 1, 3, Sch. Ved. Pass. ऋच्यते (p. ऋच्य॑मान)
to be praised, RV.
